    "markdown": "10 — makes tea sweet?\n11 — wants a piece of bread?\n12 — piece of bread is yours?\n13 — is the name of your baker?\n14 — is his shop, the one at the end of the road, or\nthe one near the post office?\n15 — understands this exercise?\n16 — of you understand this exercise?\n17 — is the answer to my question?\n18 — knows the answer?\n19 — teaches you English?\n20 — are you learning now?\n\n## 9 Telling the Time\n\n### 9.1 Elementary\n\n*Half past; (a) quarter to; ten (minutes) past.* The word *minutes* is usually omitted if a multiple of five is used.\n\n* * *\n\n● Say the following times:\n\n11.09 - 9.30 - 10.15 - 3.45 - 6.10 - 7.25 - 11.35 -\n12.45 - 1.05 - 2.50 - 6.45 - 6.40 - 4.56 - 12.00.\n\n## 10 *too* and *enough*\n\n### 10.1 Elementary\n\n*Too.* An adverb of excess; with *to* + infinitive and/or *for* + (pro)noun.\n\nThis soup is very hot; I can't drink it.\n\nThis soup is too hot (for me) to drink.*\n\nThat's a lot of money; a book like that shouldn't cost so much.\n\nThat's too much money for a book like that.\n\n(* Expect the mistake: 'This soup is too hot for me to drink it.' The infinitive, even of a transitive verb, has no",
